1
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:26,510
Black Cat Detective, please respond.

2
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,160
Dad.

3
00:00:31,710 --> 00:00:32,150
Dad.

4
00:00:32,330 --> 00:00:34,710
Mom asked me to bring this up for you.

5
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:37,560
She got it from the hospital cafeteria.

6
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:38,600
You have a weak stomach.

7
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:40,110
You have to eat on time.

8
00:00:40,110 --> 00:00:41,470
I'm going to watch you eat.

9
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:42,520
Watch me eat?

10
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,430
Okay.

11
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:46,110
Then watch Dad eat

12
00:00:46,110 --> 00:00:47,110
from outside, okay?

13
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:47,560
Okay.

14
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:49,240
Here. One, two, three.

15
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:51,790
Are you seated?

16
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:52,880
Yes.

17
00:00:56,070 --> 00:00:57,390
What's this? Pickled mustard greens?

18
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:14,540
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 16=

19
00:01:14,870 --> 00:01:16,680
I found this
in the archives this morning.

20
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:20,790
The butterfly
has flapped its wings again.

21
00:01:21,670 --> 00:01:22,850
(Autopsy Examination Record)
In 1990,

22
00:01:22,870 --> 00:01:24,870
Longfan River Body in a Box Case.

23
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:25,870
It was also an unsolved case.

24
00:01:25,870 --> 00:01:27,480
The killer is getting bolder.

25
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,400
This is a challenge to us.

26
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,710
The case file
also records a hammer blow.

27
00:01:31,710 --> 00:01:32,590
The cause of death was unknown.

28
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:34,710
If this is a serial Hammer Killer case,

29
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:36,480
we have to catch
the killer as soon as possible.

30
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:38,150
But it's been thirty years.

31
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:39,840
This person is either an old man by now,

32
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:41,400
or long dead and buried.

33
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,350
How are we supposed to catch him?

34
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:43,760
Not now.

35
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:45,640
We need to catch him back in the '90s.

36
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:55,350
There are several shallow wounds
on Zhao Qian's body,

37
00:01:55,790 --> 00:01:57,310
along with skin ulcers.

38
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:59,020
(Forensic Pathology Report)

39
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:03,840
This is bad.

40
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:05,310
He has HIV.

41
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:10,030
Qin.

42
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:11,000
Qin.

43
00:02:11,190 --> 00:02:12,240
Can you hear me, Qin?

44
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:13,310
Son. Son.

45
00:02:13,310 --> 00:02:13,710
Qin.

46
00:02:13,710 --> 00:02:14,240
Dad is calling you.

47
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:14,870
Qin.

48
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:15,960
Qin.

49
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:17,400
Can you hear me, Qin?

50
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:20,630
Qin.

51
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:21,870
Qin.

52
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,710
Can you hear me, Qin?

53
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:35,590
Qin.

54
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:37,430
Qin.

55
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:39,360
I hear you.

56
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,520
You scared me to death.

57
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:41,960
Qin.

58
00:02:42,630 --> 00:02:43,800
I thought I'd never
be able to reach you again.

59
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:44,870
Ming,

60
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:47,000
is something going to happen again?

61
00:02:47,030 --> 00:02:48,470
About Zhang Daxin having a gun,

62
00:02:49,150 --> 00:02:50,910
you had Ming tell me, didn't you?

63
00:02:51,470 --> 00:02:52,400
Thank you.

64
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,810
You saved Dad's life again.

65
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:55,060
Let's not talk about that now.

66
00:02:55,470 --> 00:02:57,000
Are you performing
an autopsy on Zhao Qian?

67
00:02:57,470 --> 00:02:58,630
He has HIV.

68
00:02:59,910 --> 00:03:01,280
Those skin ulcers

69
00:03:01,310 --> 00:03:03,190
could be infections
caused by advanced AIDS.

70
00:03:03,190 --> 00:03:04,240
Tell Mr. Zhou right away

71
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,280
to use the highest level of protection.

72
00:03:05,430 --> 00:03:06,840
Anyone who has come
into contact with the body

73
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:08,750
and has broken skin
must disinfect it thoroughly.

74
00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:11,120
All instruments and the autopsy table
must be thoroughly disinfected.

75
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:12,150
Okay. I'll...

76
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:12,630
I'll go

77
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:14,560
tell Mr. Zhou right now.

78
00:03:15,490 --> 00:03:16,260
And Dad,

79
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:19,510
I'm here.

80
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,080
The killer has probably realized

81
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,030
that we can communicate.

82
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:25,010
When Zhang Daxin's case happened,

83
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:26,840
he tried to kill me as a child

84
00:03:27,870 --> 00:03:29,440
so that I wouldn't exist in the present.

85
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,360
No wonder
someone tried to break in last night.

86
00:03:32,590 --> 00:03:33,400
Don't worry.

87
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:35,840
Dad won't let anything happen to you.

88
00:03:37,590 --> 00:03:39,120
I promised your mom

89
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:41,030
I'd protect you both
for the rest of my life.

90
00:03:41,430 --> 00:03:43,280
We'll catch this killer soon.

91
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:45,710
I'll make sure I catch him in 1990.

92
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,150
All right, I have to go.

93
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:48,910
I'm going to tell Mr. Zhou.

94
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,190
Wait.

95
00:03:55,910 --> 00:03:56,710
Stop.

96
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:00,150
Captain Qin just called.

97
00:04:00,430 --> 00:04:01,240
He said the victim

98
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:02,710
has AIDS.

99
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,430
We need to use
the highest level of protection.

100
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,590
I asked my partner.

101
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,310
Normal contact with someone who has AIDS

102
00:04:14,310 --> 00:04:15,590
is completely safe.

103
00:04:15,590 --> 00:04:17,800
But when performing an autopsy,

104
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,430
you have to be extremely careful.

105
00:04:19,430 --> 00:04:20,160
Understood.

106
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:21,160
Captain Qin.

107
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:22,310
So,

108
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:24,390
the HIV in the victim's body

109
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:25,870
is still infectious?

110
00:04:26,830 --> 00:04:29,390
The victim has only been dead
for a little over ten hours.

111
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:31,190
The HIV hasn't been inactivated yet.

112
00:04:31,390 --> 00:04:32,600
Of course it's still infectious.

113
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,270
Wait, why are you backing away?

114
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:37,950
I'm not afraid.

115
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:38,830
What would I be afraid of?

116
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:40,170
I'm worried about you.

117
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:41,870
You're the one performing the autopsy,

118
00:04:41,870 --> 00:04:42,830
not me.

119
00:04:43,090 --> 00:04:44,480
Zhou, let me remind you again.

120
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,720
While respecting the patient with AIDS,

121
00:04:47,630 --> 00:04:49,000
make sure you protect yourself.

122
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:50,070
All right.

123
00:04:51,770 --> 00:04:53,070
What else did your partner say?

124
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:56,440
He reviewed
your external examination report

125
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:57,800
and has basically reached a conclusion.

126
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,630
He'll tell you after the autopsy.

127
00:04:59,630 --> 00:05:00,360
Understood.

128
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,040
He doesn't want
to influence my judgment.

129
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:03,600
Your partner is very professional.

130
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,600
You two...

131
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:07,630
Okay.

132
00:05:07,630 --> 00:05:08,560
We're ready to begin.

133
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:11,310
Thank you.

134
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:12,000
All right.

135
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,270
We're ready to begin.

136
00:05:13,270 --> 00:05:13,920
Okay.

137
00:05:14,830 --> 00:05:16,140
Tell me,

138
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:18,550
if the killer is still alive,

139
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,600
what is he doing now?

140
00:05:20,190 --> 00:05:21,870
Can he really live with what he's done?

141
00:05:24,430 --> 00:05:25,360
I don't know either.

142
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:28,040
I don't know what other dangers
Qin might face.

143
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,000
But like you said,

144
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:33,480
Captain Qin didn't live to the present,

145
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:36,190
so the killer might not
have lived this long either.

146
00:05:36,830 --> 00:05:38,190
Maybe he already died from an illness.

147
00:05:41,870 --> 00:05:43,040
What I can be sure of is

148
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:46,040
the serial murders
in 1990 are still happening.

149
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:49,160
This person must still be alive.

150
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:59,040
All three major A-share indexes
opened higher before turning negative.

151
00:05:59,160 --> 00:05:59,830
As of this report,

152
00:05:59,830 --> 00:06:01,510
the Shanghai Composite Index
is down 0.37%.

153
00:06:01,510 --> 00:06:04,000
The Shenzhen Component Index
is down 0.68%.

154
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,120
The ChiNext Index is down 0.50%.

155
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:08,800
More than 4,300 stocks
across the market are down.

156
00:06:22,390 --> 00:06:22,920
Captain Qin.

157
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:24,260
We're done.

158
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:27,360
How did it go?

159
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:29,160
The autopsy is complete.

160
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,370
There were no abnormalities
in the victim's internal organs.

161
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:34,070
But his stomach and intestines
were completely empty.

162
00:06:36,390 --> 00:06:38,070
That means he hadn't
eaten anything before he died.

163
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:39,860
For at least twelve hours,

164
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:40,750
he hadn't eaten.

165
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,850
What about his back and butt...

166
00:06:42,850 --> 00:06:43,640
Buttocks.

167
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:47,160
His buttocks
and thighs were all injured.

168
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:48,360
Those weren't livor mortis, right?

169
00:06:48,750 --> 00:06:50,000
Right.

170
00:06:50,490 --> 00:06:51,950
They were all injuries,
not livor mortis.

171
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,240
Injuries and livor mortis
are easy to distinguish.

172
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:55,590
The victim

173
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:57,690
was curled up

174
00:06:57,700 --> 00:06:58,640
and lying on his side.

175
00:06:58,740 --> 00:07:01,120
So the livor mortis
was all on his right side.

176
00:07:01,190 --> 00:07:02,250
That's a lot of bruising.

177
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:04,040
He was badly injured.

178
00:07:07,530 --> 00:07:08,220
Qin.

179
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:10,360
I know the cause of death.

180
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,070
Good.

181
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:13,390
Then I can tell you

182
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,120
what my partner thinks.

183
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:17,190
Based on Mr. Zhou's findings,

184
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,720
we can basically confirm

185
00:07:18,870 --> 00:07:20,630
that the victim died of crush syndrome.

186
00:07:20,630 --> 00:07:21,360
Crush syndrome?

187
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:22,920
It doesn't necessarily
mean death from compression.

188
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,750
Prolonged physical abuse

189
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:25,800
can also cause

190
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,390
extensive damage to deep tissues.

191
00:07:27,390 --> 00:07:29,190
We call this cause of death

192
00:07:29,430 --> 00:07:30,510
crush syndrome.

193
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:32,720
But to confirm it,

194
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:34,040
we have to wait
until the autopsy is complete

195
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:36,430
and rule out organic disease
of the internal organs

196
00:07:36,430 --> 00:07:37,750
or other hidden causes.

197
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:40,160
The truth can only
be based on solid evidence.

198
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:42,190
He's right.

199
00:07:42,390 --> 00:07:44,830
Zhao Qian's cause of death
was crush syndrome.

200
00:07:44,870 --> 00:07:46,600
He was beaten to death.

201
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:47,720
Qin,

202
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,430
how is your partner so good at this?

203
00:07:52,390 --> 00:07:53,630
The way he thinks

204
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,750
is so advanced and meticulous.

205
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:56,430
I feel

206
00:07:56,430 --> 00:07:58,390
like I didn't
study hard enough in school.

207
00:07:58,830 --> 00:08:00,190
How did I not think of that?

208
00:08:03,870 --> 00:08:04,920
A patient

209
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,750
was beaten to death.

210
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,950
He didn't even
get a full meal before he died.

211
00:08:12,830 --> 00:08:13,630
Captain Qin,

212
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,920
how could the killer
do something like this?

213
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:17,560
But

214
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:19,630
come to think of it,

215
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,870
what did Zhao Qian do

216
00:08:21,870 --> 00:08:23,120
to make someone hate him this much?

217
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,510
Thanks for your hard work, Zhou.

218
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:29,000
The Physical Evidence Unit's
report is out.

219
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,080
The box was basically soaked through,

220
00:08:33,270 --> 00:08:34,660
so no fingerprints were left.

221
00:08:34,730 --> 00:08:35,810
But after the Physical Evidence Unit

222
00:08:36,250 --> 00:08:37,690
dried the box,

223
00:08:37,690 --> 00:08:39,750
they found glove prints around it.

224
00:08:39,750 --> 00:08:40,970
And at the bottom of the box,

225
00:08:40,970 --> 00:08:42,630
there were traces of cement particles.

226
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:44,020
They believe

227
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:46,380
the killer was wearing gloves
with cement on them

228
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:47,900
when the box was pushed into the water.

229
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:49,780
So there were probably two killers,

230
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:51,940
and they most likely
didn't use a vehicle.

231
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:54,700
They carried the box
all the way to the river and dumped it.

232
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:55,700
Is that what you're saying?

233
00:08:57,220 --> 00:08:58,620
The Longfan River is so long,

234
00:08:59,060 --> 00:09:00,380
with so many tributaries and branches.

235
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:01,980
How are we supposed to know

236
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:03,540
where they dumped the body?

237
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:12,820
Now we know the victim's time of death

238
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:16,020
and the flow rate of the Longfan River.

239
00:09:17,940 --> 00:09:19,100
Go to the meteorological bureau.

240
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:21,740
Check the wind speed that day

241
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:23,660
and the water level
of the Longfan River.

242
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:26,540
Then we can roughly determine
where the body was dumped.

243
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:29,540
But we don't know
when the body was dumped.

244
00:09:29,620 --> 00:09:31,220
To calculate where it was dumped,

245
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:33,020
we need to know

246
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:34,700
the exact time
the body entered the water.

247
00:09:34,900 --> 00:09:36,700
Knowing only the victim's time of death

248
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:37,580
doesn't help.

249
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:40,620
I have an idea.

250
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:42,940
It's just a little crude.

251
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:45,540
How crude?

252
00:09:48,940 --> 00:09:50,020
With your IQ,

253
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:51,900
there's no point telling you.

254
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:54,780
What's wrong with my IQ?

255
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:56,220
My IQ is just fine, Captain Qin.

256
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:58,420
I was one of the top students in school.

257
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:00,580
Captain Qin,

258
00:10:00,780 --> 00:10:02,420
I have to admit, you're good.

259
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:03,900
Why didn't I think

260
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:06,260
of using a pig instead
of a body for the experiment?

261
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:08,620
Mainly because your weight
doesn't match Zhao Qian's.

262
00:10:08,620 --> 00:10:10,060
Otherwise,
I'd use you for the experiment.

263
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:11,900
Well, you don't need me.

264
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:13,300
Couldn't we just use bricks?

265
00:10:13,540 --> 00:10:15,340
Wouldn't bricks just sink?

266
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:16,660
I've already checked.

267
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:17,380
Today...

268
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:20,020
Can you walk properly?

269
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:20,440
Sorry.

270
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:21,700
Sorry, Captain Qin. Sorry.

271
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:23,700
Today, the Longfan River's flow rate,

272
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:24,980
wind speed, and water level

273
00:10:25,140 --> 00:10:26,700
are about the same
as they were on the day of the crime.

274
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:27,860
We just need to calculate

275
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:29,780
how long it takes for this box,
weighing about the same as Zhao Qian,

276
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:31,180
to become soaked to the same waterline.

277
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:32,300
Then we can roughly calculate

278
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:33,580
how far it drifted.

279
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:36,380
Understand?

280
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:38,500
Of course I do.

281
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:40,220
I'm just worried
there might be some error.

282
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:41,820
Even if there is, it doesn't matter.

283
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:42,700
At worst,

284
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:44,820
we'll search the area around
the point indicated by the experiment

285
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:45,860
as well.

286
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:47,900
Then we should be able to roughly
determine where the body was dumped.

287
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:52,860
What are you bending over like that for?

288
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:55,940
I'm checking the waterline.

289
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:57,300
Here.

290
00:10:57,780 --> 00:10:58,860
Look a little farther ahead.

291
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:00,140
Move left.

292
00:11:00,340 --> 00:11:01,740
Left. Look to the left.

293
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:03,140
See it?

294
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:04,860
Right.

295
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:05,700
Look farther left.

296
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:06,740
I can't see the box.

297
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:08,700
Look. See what you can spot.

298
00:11:09,060 --> 00:11:10,300
You want me to look at the ripples?

299
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:10,940
Right.

300
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:12,940
With the wind blowing this way,

301
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:15,780
I think the box could drift pretty far.

302
00:11:15,980 --> 00:11:17,300
Captain, you...

303
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:20,060
Captain Qin.

304
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:22,500
Why do you
always leave without telling me?

305
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:32,300
(A very large washing machine box,
half submerged and half above water)

306
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:33,300
Section Chief Qin.

307
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:34,620
Come look at this.

308
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:37,740
Don't you think this looks like

309
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:39,260
our Body in a Box Case?

310
00:11:39,540 --> 00:11:41,700
(Strange box drifting down the Longfan River)
The box kept bobbing up and down.

311
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,140
It looked really eerie.

312
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:44,820
It didn't look empty.

313
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:48,100
Bobbing.

314
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:50,340
Draft.

315
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:00,180
Lift.

316
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:01,740
Ma, put some muscle into it.

317
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:05,580
Put it here.

318
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:06,420
Easy.

319
00:12:09,180 --> 00:12:09,940
How is it?

320
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:10,660
Captain.

321
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:12,460
The waterline is just right.

322
00:12:13,140 --> 00:12:15,500
It took about five or six hours.

323
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:17,300
The distance is about six kilometers.

324
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:19,340
It passed a pier,

325
00:12:19,540 --> 00:12:20,540
an old residential area,

326
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:21,700
and riverside villas.

327
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:23,300
The terrain is pretty complicated.

328
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:24,700
It'll take us a while to investigate.

329
00:12:25,340 --> 00:12:26,300
Let's start checking the area.

330
00:12:26,860 --> 00:12:27,660
Captain.

331
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:29,060
This pig...

332
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:31,340
I'll contact the cafeteria tonight.

333
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:32,940
We can have something good to eat.

334
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:34,060
We can't do that.

335
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:35,220
According to regulations,

336
00:12:35,340 --> 00:12:37,380
all experimental pigs
must be disposed of safely.

337
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:38,060
Understand?

338
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:38,780
Understand?

339
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:40,340
Go eat grass.

340
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:42,100
Lift the box.

341
00:12:44,940 --> 00:12:46,020
I have to carry it myself?

342
00:12:57,940 --> 00:13:00,500
(The box drifted for about five hours.)

343
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:02,740
(Estimated distance is six kilometers.)

344
00:13:04,340 --> 00:13:05,140
Captain Qin.

345
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:06,780
Based on this,

346
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:08,660
near where the box entered
the water, there's a pier,

347
00:13:08,940 --> 00:13:09,860
an old residential area,

348
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:10,700
and riverside villas.

349
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:12,540
The people
in the area are pretty diverse.

350
00:13:12,740 --> 00:13:14,020
It'll take us a while to investigate.

351
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:19,020
We're still going?

352
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:21,180
We've been digging all day.

353
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:22,820
We haven't found a thing.

354
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:26,220
That guide said there were
Republican-era silver dollars here.

355
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:29,130
I think it was just clickbait.

356
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:33,580
Enough.

357
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:35,980
How about a ghost story
to keep us awake?

358
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:39,740
It's not a ghost story.

359
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:40,700
It's a true story.

360
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:42,380
I heard the old folks talk
about it when I was a kid.

361
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:43,740
Back in the '90s,

362
00:13:43,940 --> 00:13:47,360
there was a small white building
upstream on the Longfan River.

363
00:13:47,380 --> 00:13:48,580
A small white building?

364
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:50,220
A detached two-story building

365
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:51,390
by the river.

366
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:53,060
They said no one lived there,

367
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:55,380
but the lights often came on
in the middle of the night.

368
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:57,420
Legend has it

369
00:13:57,740 --> 00:13:58,820
that inside...

370
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:01,060
What was inside?

371
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:03,820
One of the walls

372
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,060
was filled with gold bars.

373
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:07,300
What happened after that?

374
00:14:07,340 --> 00:14:08,500
No one ever found them.

375
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:10,460
Maybe they were taken away long ago.

376
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:11,900
Or maybe

377
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:13,940
they were never there to begin with.

378
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:16,160
(The small white building upstream
on the Longfan River in 1990)

379
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:17,840
(had walls filled with gold bars)

380
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:24,300
If there's even
a shred of truth to this rumor,

381
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:26,860
then in Longfan in the '90s,

382
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:28,980
what kind of situation

383
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,500
could have involved so much gold?

384
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:40,380
Our night owl is finally home.

385
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:42,180
I thought

386
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:43,700
the Dragon King of the Longfan River

387
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,060
had taken you as his son-in-law.

388
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:46,300
Nonsense.

389
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:47,500
I'm exhausted.

390
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:52,500
Dad,

391
00:14:52,860 --> 00:14:55,460
your eyes are as red as a rabbit's.

392
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:57,660
Have you ever seen
a rabbit this handsome?

393
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:00,980
With one of us a doctor

394
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:01,860
and the other a police officer,

395
00:15:02,060 --> 00:15:04,260
we're lucky
if we even get to see each other.

396
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:05,780
I'll take him to Mrs. Huang's.

397
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:07,060
You,

398
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:08,740
right now,

399
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:09,980
go get some sleep.

400
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:11,340
Look at your face.

401
00:15:11,730 --> 00:15:13,740
You don't look much better
than my post-op patients.

402
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:15,460
Go on.

403
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:16,180
I'm leaving.

404
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,180
Once you've had some rest,

405
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:22,820
go get something hot at the cafeteria.

406
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:24,540
Don't always eat instant noodles.

407
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:25,820
Take care of your stomach.

408
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:27,980
I'm off.

409
00:15:44,180 --> 00:15:44,980
Ming.

410
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:47,940
Dad.

411
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:49,740
I've been waiting for you all night.

412
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:52,300
Zhao Qian's cause of death
was exactly what you said.

413
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:53,500
Then we ran an experiment

414
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,060
and narrowed down
where the body was dumped.

415
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:56,860
We searched the area all night.

416
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:58,980
Now we've finally
narrowed down the target area.

417
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:00,180
But the tricky part is

418
00:16:00,780 --> 00:16:02,540
it's in the riverside villa area
on Guanjing Road,

419
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:05,060
on the west bank of the Longfan River.

420
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:06,260
The biggest problem is

421
00:16:06,540 --> 00:16:07,660
the area is highly private,

422
00:16:07,780 --> 00:16:09,580
so a routine investigation
is relatively slow.

423
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:11,460
We've made a major discovery here.

424
00:16:11,500 --> 00:16:12,940
By cross-referencing big data,

425
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:14,020
we've pinpointed a location.

426
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:16,500
Wait, I didn't quite understand.

427
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:16,900
You...

428
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:19,940
What kind of show
are you watching over there now?

429
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:21,420
The most popular
TV series here right now

430
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:23,660
is Yearnings.

431
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:26,620
It's actually a way
of filtering information nowadays.

432
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:30,020
So TV shows and big data

433
00:16:30,020 --> 00:16:31,420
aren't the same thing, right?

434
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:33,340
In other words,
a TV show can't solve a case,

435
00:16:33,340 --> 00:16:35,420
but big data can help solve one.

436
00:16:35,420 --> 00:16:36,540
Am I understanding that right?

437
00:16:36,860 --> 00:16:37,660
That's right, Dad.

438
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:39,100
You have to keep up with the times.

439
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:40,900
Would you say

440
00:16:40,900 --> 00:16:42,260
that in my time,

441
00:16:42,260 --> 00:16:43,900
I'm already

442
00:16:44,540 --> 00:16:46,700
pretty forward-thinking?

443
00:16:46,780 --> 00:16:47,580
Definitely.

444
00:16:47,660 --> 00:16:49,140
After all, you've got me
as your secret weapon.

445
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:50,100
By the way,

446
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:51,260
we found

447
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:53,620
a detached white villa
at No. 17 Guanjing Road.

448
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:55,300
People in our time
call it the Little White Villa.

449
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:56,060
Earlier,

450
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:58,020
you said the Economic Crime Investigation Unit
couldn't trace the accounts.

451
00:16:58,180 --> 00:16:58,940
This place

452
00:16:58,940 --> 00:17:00,060
might be a secret location

453
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:01,580
where the Urban Construction Group
hid the money,

454
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:03,940
or a safe house
for one of its key figures.

455
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:04,980
If the location

456
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:06,260
was the same back in the '90s,

457
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:07,300
you should be able to

458
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:08,380
find key clues there.

459
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:09,900
No. 17 Guanjing Road.

460
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,540
Doesn't that match the area

461
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:12,740
we've narrowed down?

462
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:15,260
But we still can't determine
the exact address.

463
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:17,300
These are only deductions
based on historical information.

464
00:17:17,460 --> 00:17:18,260
Fortunately,

465
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:19,780
the internet has a long memory.

466
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:21,900
If we can verify who owns this house,

467
00:17:22,220 --> 00:17:24,060
we might find some key information.

468
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:27,940
I think I basically understand.

469
00:17:40,220 --> 00:17:40,740
Li.

470
00:17:41,620 --> 00:17:42,180
Li.

471
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:46,340
Nice reflexes.

472
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:47,300
Come with me.

473
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,420
Wait, Captain. What are you doing?

474
00:17:49,740 --> 00:17:51,380
I was dreaming
about catching the killer.

475
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:53,340
I was just about to catch him.

476
00:17:54,260 --> 00:17:56,820
That place
could very well be the crime scene.

477
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:58,740
I need to ask Chief Zhao
for a search warrant.

478
00:17:58,740 --> 00:17:59,740
Maybe if we follow this lead,

479
00:17:59,740 --> 00:18:01,020
we can also help
the Economic Crime Investigation Unit

480
00:18:01,340 --> 00:18:03,220
solve that Urban Construction

481
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:04,380
fundraising case.

482
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:05,700
How are you going to search it?

483
00:18:06,180 --> 00:18:07,860
Zhao left
for a meeting early this morning.

484
00:18:08,180 --> 00:18:09,260
He won't be back until this afternoon.

485
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:14,580
How about this?

486
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:16,420
Let's get some solid information first.

487
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:17,900
We'll report
to Chief Zhao when he gets back.

488
00:18:18,030 --> 00:18:18,850
Let's go.

489
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:20,420
What are you waiting for?

490
00:18:24,070 --> 00:18:24,840
Morning, Zhuang.

491
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:26,860
By the way,

492
00:18:27,580 --> 00:18:28,540
Zhou has saved

493
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:30,020
quite a few boxes for you too.

494
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:31,020
Remember to pick them up.

495
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:35,500
Thank you, Captain Qin.

496
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:40,860
Stay safe.

497
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:50,680
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

498
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:58,520
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

499
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:06,600
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

500
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:12,480
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

501
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:22,440
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

502
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:28,120
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

503
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:38,480
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

504
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:44,320
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

505
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:53,920
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

506
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:59,640
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

507
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:09,480
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

508
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:17,000
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

509
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:21,640
♪Can you hear me?♪

510
00:20:21,640 --> 00:20:25,440
♪Can you hear me?♪

511
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:32,880
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

512
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:40,640
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

513
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:46,560
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

514
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:52,040
♪After all these years♪

515
00:20:54,560 --> 00:21:02,040
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

516
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:04,240
♪And tell you♪

517
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:08,720
♪I haven't let you down♪
